# Commit Workflow

When the user says **"Run the Commit Workflow"** (or "commit this", "prepare a
commit"), follow the canonical, ordered procedure in **`COMMIT_WORKFLOW.md`** at
the repo root. Do not improvise a different order.

Key points (see `COMMIT_WORKFLOW.md` for the full steps):

- Assess state and **ask about anything ambiguous** (version scheme, feature vs fix).
- Add/verify unit tests for new functionality **and** legacy-data compatibility;
  **boot a simulator first** (`xcrun simctl boot <iPhone udid>`) or tests report
  "TEST FAILED / No result" for every test with no crash log.
- Run all tests; if any fail, add tests around that area and fix.
- Refactor obvious duplication (no SwiftLint configured — rely on compiler warnings).
- Bump the version in `project.pbxproj` (`MARKETING_VERSION` / `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION`).
- Full clean build (`xcodebuild clean build`).
- Update docs: `prompts/YYYY-MM-DD-*.md` (verbatim prompts + `## Pickup Context`),
  MEMORY.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, SPEC.md.
- **Stage once**, then commit with a conventional message and the trailer
  `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>`, then push.

`SPEC.md` is the live plan tracker — update its status markers and Progress
Summary table for anything shipped this session.
